---
title: Introduction
description: NeoWorks is a personal cloud built on ownership, not surveillance. One identity, seven apps, your data.
---

NeoWorks is a personal cloud platform. You get one identity and a single subscription
that unlocks seven first-party apps — files, contacts, calendar, tasks, passwords,
sharing, and trips — all backed by storage that belongs to **you**, not a tech giant.

Everything is open source and self-hostable. Run it on our infrastructure, or run your
own node and own the whole stack.

## What you get

- **One identity** — a single OAuth 2.0 account across every app and device.
- **Seven apps** — Grove, Vault, Vine, Tide, Twig, Relay, and Trail.
- **End-to-end encryption** — Vault secrets and shared media are encrypted client-side.
- **Real-time sync** — changes fan out across your devices over NATS JetStream.
- **A developer platform** — build third-party apps and earn a share of every Pro split.

## How it fits together

The platform is a small set of Go services in front of SurrealDB:

- **oauth** — issues tokens, hosts the cross-origin Vault crypto sandbox.
- **api** — the GraphQL data plane; enforces row-level isolation in the database.
- **assets** — public, cached asset delivery (encrypted media is handled separately).

Apps never read raw key material. All crypto runs inside the cross-origin Vault iframe
and is brokered over `postMessage`, so a compromised app cannot exfiltrate your keys.

### Storage model

Each user's rows are isolated at the SurrealDB layer. Scopes granted to an OAuth client
are enforced by the database, not by application middleware — a stolen token can only do
what it was explicitly granted.

